---
title: Lamb radiatore
servings: 8
yield: 8 to 12 servings
tags: [italian, lamb, braise, make-ahead]
cuisine: italian
source: Lamb Radiatore by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/lamb-radiatore
---

== Braised lamb ==

Season the @lamb shanks{5%lb} with @salt{}, @black pepper{} and a little
@sugar{}. Refrigerate overnight.

Heat a convection oven to 275°F. Heat @olive oil{} in a #braising pan{} over
medium-high heat until it smokes, brown the shanks well, and set them aside.

Pour off the oil and return the pan to the heat. Brown the @onion{2}(in large dice) and @carrot{1}(in large dice). Add the @garlic{4%cloves}(smashed)
and cook ~{2%minutes}.

Add the @celery{2%stalks}(in large dice), @anchovy fillets{4} and
@dry white wine{3%cup}. Boil until the pan is almost dry.

Add the @beef stock{16%cup}(1 gallon) and bring to a boil. Take off the heat,
return the shanks, cover, and braise in the oven ~{3%hours}, until the meat is
coming off the bone. Cool the shanks in the liquid overnight.

Lift out the shanks and pull the meat. Strain the liquid into a pot, discard
the solids, and reduce over low heat ~{1%hour}. Cool, and pour it over the
meat.

== To serve ==

Put a large pot of salted water on to boil.

Heat @olive oil{} in a #rondeau{} over medium-high heat until it smokes. Add
the @carrot{1}(finely diced), @celery root{1}(finely diced) and
@white onion{1}(finely diced), season with salt, and cook ~{1-2%minutes}
without colour. Take off the heat, add the lamb and its liquid, and bring to a
boil.

Boil the @radiatore pasta{2%lb} ~{2-3%minutes}. Drain into the rondeau, keeping some
of the pasta water.

After ~{2-3%minutes}, add the @mint leaves{1%oz}(cut into small squares) and
half the @pecorino cheese{4%oz}(grated). Loosen with pasta water as needed.
Serve with the rest of the pecorino on top.

> The short boil assumes fresh radiatore; dried needs its full package time.
